WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.939
Being a D-Class for the SCP Foundation is
a lot like playing Russian roulette: One day,

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:10.481
you could be assigned to a tickle fight with
a friendly blob of slime, and the next you’re

00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:16.090
getting your femurs broken to lure a sadistic
old man back into his containment chamber.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:22.499
So, when D-9781 was told to simply sit in
an interrogation room and wait, he really

00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:23.910
didn’t know what to think.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.689
But the last thing he probably expected to
see when the door behind him creaked open

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:31.339
was for a well-dressed stranger to step in.

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:36.250
This man wasn’t like any member of Foundation
staff the D-Class had ever seen: He was a

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.239
short, Caucasian man with a receding hairline
and a neat black mustache.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:45.390
Instead of the standard lab coat and shirt
normally seen around the facility, this man

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:52.120
wore a black waistcoat, a pair of white gloves,
and a wry smile that betrayed a sinister intent.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.379
He looked like a butler – and not just any
butler, but the quintessential butler.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:01.690
If you were asked to doodle a cartoon butler,
this would be the man you drew.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.390
The D-Class almost laughed in sheer confusion.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:08.170
He had no idea that, in a mere moment, he
would be dead.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.680
“What’s the deal with Jeeves?”

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.470
He asked with a mocking half-smile, but he
didn’t get to hear a response.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.720
The Butler approached at frightening speeds.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.360
The D-Class, in his last moments on this earth,
saw the glint of something metallic under

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.850
the overhead lights, moving too fast for him
to see what it was, and then felt a sharp

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.520
pain across his throat.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.310
The Butler was standing beside him now, still
with that wry little smile.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.509
The D-Class could see now that the Butler
was carrying a small buck knife, dripping

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:37.670
with red.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:41.840
Just as he was piecing together what had happened
to him, the D-Class collapsed onto the table

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.990
he was sitting at, his throat expertly slit.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:50.039
His grisly task completed, the Butler gave
a polite nod, and exited the room – smiling

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:52.509
at the Foundation guards standing outside.

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:54.390
Who is this man?

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.100
Why is he dressed like this?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:01.100
And most importantly, why is he allowed to
murder D-Class personnel on Foundation grounds

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.729
without consequence?

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:07.780
We can answer that first question right now
- because this isn’t a man at all, he’s

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:14.430
the anomalous product of SCP – 662, also
known as The Butler’s Hand Bell.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.540
First we need to go back to the beginning,
and see how this anomalous object first fell

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.340
into the hands of the SCP Foundation.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:26.010
Like a lot of anomalous objects now under
the care of the Foundation, its true origins

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:30.129
remain mysterious, and it spent quite some
time underground.

00:02:30.129 --> 00:02:35.069
We mean that literally, by the way - it was
buried with its last owner, a man whose name

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:38.069
has since been redacted from Foundation files.

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:42.290
Clutched in this unknown man’s skeletal
hand, it was extremely likely that the bell

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.550
might never have been seen again.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:50.090
But then a petty thief and grave robber by
the name of George Dixon came along and dug

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.159
up the grave.

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:56.170
A simple, greedy act that has changed a number
of people’s lives forever.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:01.190
Not knowing the true value of what he held,
Mr. Dixon made his way to a pawnshop for his

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.190
payday.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.659
There, the store owner made the mistake of
lifting up and ringing the bell.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:10.440
As if on cue, he heard footsteps approaching
behind him.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.460
The store owner turned and gasped.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:16.260
He saw a complete stranger emerging from the
stock-room behind him.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.510
He was a short, well-dressed man, smiling
as he advanced towards him.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.490
The proprietor of the pawnshop didn’t know
who this guy with the strange outfit was,

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.610
but he assumed he was an accomplice of the
man in his store and that the two were trying

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.860
to rob him.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:34.080
He grabbed a shotgun from underneath his counter,
turned to The Butler and blasted him in the

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.799
chest with both barrels.

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:41.069
The Butler fell back, dead, and George Dixon
fled the scene in a blind panic.

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:46.000
Contrary to what the owner may have believed,
nothing that’d happened here had been planned.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.110
Dixon was just as surprised as he was to see
this mysterious Butler emerge from the stockroom.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.950
So what had just happened?

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.360
The pawn shop owner reported the incident
to the authorities and the Butler’s body

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:01.500
was taken to the local morgue, while the silver
bell ended up in a police evidence locker.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:07.519
Later that same night, things went from a
strange bungled robbery to a full-on anomaly,

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:10.660
attracting the attention of the SCP Foundation.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.870
First, the Butler's body disappeared from
the morgue the second the mortician took her

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.980
eyes off of it, and then reappeared, now alive,
in the police storage locker.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.980
Why?

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.680
Because an unwitting sergeant just so happened
to ring the little silver bell.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.000
Agent Bradford of the SCP Foundation was promptly
on the scene.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.480
He pretended to be an FBI Agent, and escorted
The Butler off of the premises - claiming

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:39.050
that this was a notorious escape artist who
was wanted for federal crimes in several states.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:43.140
Things didn’t go as Bradford planned though,
when he discovered that The Butler had disappeared

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.770
from his handcuffs when no one was looking.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:49.510
Agent Bradford theorized that this had to
have something to do with the bell, and he

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.080
confiscated it for testing.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:56.250
Later, when he rang the bell inside an SCP
Containment Facility, The Butler turned up

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.420
once more.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:02.160
He introduced himself as Mr. Deeds and said
that he would happily perform any service

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.280
that Agent Bradford required.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:09.370
Despite being offered the phenomenal power
of a seemingly magical butler, Bradford politely

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.390
refused the offer and instead handed the bell
over to his superiors.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:18.150
But don’t worry, Agent Bradford wasn’t
left completely empty handed and was given

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:23.580
the esteemed SCP Foundation “Pat On The
Back” award for performing such a professional

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.370
and selfless act in service of the Foundation.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:32.980
The superior who ended up with the bell, however,
wouldn’t have quite the same level of professionalism.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.840
But more on that later.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:41.780
The bell, catalogued as SCP - 662, was small
and made of pure silver, with no obvious anomalous

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.260
elements at face value.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:48.450
It was a mere four centimeters tall and two
centimeters wide, with a small inscription

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.720
reading “Forever Mine – S.J.W.”

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.790
Researchers studying the bell also noted that
it lacked its ringer, but whenever the bell

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:03.310
was rung, a chime would still sound from somewhere
in the room to signal the arrival of Mr. Deeds,

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:04.850
the anomalous Butler.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:10.110
The object was classified as Safe, and was
kept in High Value Storage locker 23C between

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.580
uses for experiments.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:16.280
It’s an extremely low-maintenance anomaly,
with the only real requirement being a regular

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:19.100
polish to keep the silver from tarnishing
over time.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:25.960
But what of Mr. Deeds, the mysterious Butler
summoned every time someone rings SCP - 662?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.910
The Foundation needed to find out more, so
he was placed under the watchful eye of Foundation

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:36.150
researcher Dr. Mirth, who performed the first
interview with Mr. Deeds.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:41.130
As you can probably expect from such a classy
servant, Mr. Deeds was unfailingly polite

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.340
during the interview.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:47.650
He always addressed Dr. Mirth as Sir, and
was extremely accommodating - within reason.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:52.370
Mr. Deeds’ true name, birthplace, and date
of birth were still a mystery to him.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.810
He could only vaguely remember that he was
of English ancestry, and that during the time

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:01.200
of his childhood, the horse and buggy was
the most popular form of transport.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:06.460
When asked about personal details or his past,
Mr. Deeds would often appear to become distressed,

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.150
before apologizing for his inability to remember
the details.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:14.670
The most important piece of information that
Dr. Mirth obtained early on in the interview

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:20.970
was the primary function of Mr. Deeds: He
was an entity that quite literally lived to

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:21.970
serve.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:26.080
Like a genie being summoned from his lamp,
Mr. Deeds would try to perform any task that

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.470
the summoner gave him - whether it was cooking
dinner or robbing banks.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:35.150
There were certain limits to these powers
though, and these limits were what Dr. Mirth

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:36.360
needed to discover.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:40.370
Dr. Mirth first asked for a glass of iced
tea from Mr. Deeds.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.260
The Butler happily obliged, and left the room,
walking down the hallway.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:49.080
While attending agents kept their eyes on
him, Mr. Deeds continued to merely walk.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:53.570
However, the second they looked away, the
cameras observing him malfunctioned, Deeds

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:57.890
briefly disappeared, and then returned with
a tray of iced tea.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:02.240
Dr. Mirth remarked that it was perhaps the
best iced tea he’d ever tasted.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.550
Mr. Deeds couldn’t recall how the tea was
made though, or how he obtained it.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:13.390
Dr. Mirth next asked for a bar of gold at
99.98% purity, and Mr. Deeds delivered almost

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.570
the exact level of purity Dr. Mirth asked
for.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:21.970
From this, he deduced that Mr. Deeds can only
perform his teleportation and manifestation

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:25.590
abilities when he’s out of people’s direct
lines of sight.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.920
He soon discovered that certain requests were
off the table though.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:34.729
Dr. Mirth asked for Mr. Deeds to fetch him
a blue 1963 Corvette convertible.

00:08:34.729 --> 00:08:38.770
Mr. Deeds did not immediately procure the
car, instead telling the doctor that such

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:43.070
a thing was impossible because there were
too many impractical steps involved in getting

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.070
the vehicle.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:47.880
Dr. Mirth was disappointed by this, since
he really wanted that car.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.250
It seemed as though Mr. Deeds’ powers, while
enhanced by teleportation and the ability

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:57.730
to manifest simple objects, are limited by
things that a mostly normal, and very persistent

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.980
person could conceivably do.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:04.700
For example, on Dr. Mirth’s orders, Mr.
Deeds politely declined to assassinate an

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:09.830
insurgent leader in the Middle East - seeing
as he was too well-guarded and very far away.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.260
However, when given the command, he was more
than willing to head into the next room and

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.670
murder a member of D-Class with a knife.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:21.410
Dr. Mirth was interested in getting a closer
look at what was going on with Mr. Deeds’

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.680
biology, and so asked him to slit his own
throat with the same knife he used to murder

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:26.990
the D-Class.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:31.680
Mr. Deeds politely obliged, commenting before
he did to Dr. Mirth that it’d been an absolute

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.220
pleasure serving him.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.460
The body was kept within an agent’s line
of sight at all time until the autopsy could

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.240
be performed, just to make sure it didn’t
disappear.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.000
The autopsy showed that there was nothing
inherently anomalous about the physiology

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:50.860
of Mr. Deeds, and he would appear, as good
as new, the next time that the bell rang.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:53.810
Things took an even stranger turn after that
though.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:57.570
Despite it appearing like the Foundation now
knew everything they needed to know about

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:03.890
Mr. Deeds and the SCP - 662 bell, Dr. Mirth
insisted on performing further studies into

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.880
what exactly Mr. Deeds was capable of.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:11.870
For example, he requested a deep tissue massage,
and found that it completely cured his back

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:12.870
pain.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:17.250
Dr. Mirth also asked Mr. Deeds to clean his
car, and found that it was cleaned to a truly

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.390
impeccable standard.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:24.220
During his tenure as the lead researcher on
the 662 project, he also asked to receive

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:29.680
a haircut from Mr. Deeds - and found out that
while Mr. Deeds excelled at many tasks, he

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.310
made a pretty bad barber.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.780
He was great at laundry though.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:38.190
Dr. Mirth was eventually removed from 662
duty by the O5 Council, once it became clear

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:43.300
his “research” had just become an excuse
for Mr. Deeds to do errands and chores for

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.300
him.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.130
Of course, Mr. Deeds had no complaints either
way.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.521
Whether it’s serving up delicious tea, cleaning
a certain selfish researchers’ home, or

00:10:51.521 --> 00:10:58.110
murdering a D-Class personnel with a buck
knife, one thing cannot be denied - Mr. Deeds

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.880
is one hell of a Butler.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:06.350
Now go watch “SCP - 066 - Eric’s Toy”
and “SCP - 4999 - Someone To Watch Over

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:10.570
Us Tale.” for more of the best stories straight
from the SCP foundation!

